## Cryptography applications

Cryptography is the art of encoding and decoding messages with codes that are hard to decode. The codes are called "encryptions" and "decryptions." This is accomplished by using a code to encrypt and a code to decrypt. You will need to make sure that you can encrypt and decrypt messages using the codes. It's good to be able to encrypt and decrypt messages!

It is useful to be able to encrypt and decrypt messages because that enables you to use one piece of encrypted information to encrypt another piece of encrypted information. The encrypted message can then be used to encrypt a message and send it to someone else. The other person can use the encrypted message to decrypt the message and send it to you. That's how you can send encrypted messages to each other. That's how you can exchange information!

You will be learning how to encrypt and decrypt messages in the book.

